WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
So, you want to start a YouTube channel.

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:06.200
First of all, congratulations, but now

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.720
you're stuck. Making your first video

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.200
seems daunting. There's a lot of

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.960
unknowns, and you may not feel ready.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.120
But, here's the truth. You do not have

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.960
to be ready. My brother Zach is 50 years

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.760
old. He never recorded anything before.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.320
He didn't know how to edit, barely knew

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.840
how to use his phone, but he made his

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:24.440
first YouTube video anyways. Less than a

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.680
month later, he was making $214 in a

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.520
single day, and he was monetized on

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.840
YouTube. Because your first video

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.240
doesn't have to be perfect, it just has

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.240
to exist. And today I'm going to be

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:36.360
breaking down the exact nine steps that

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.400
he used to make his first YouTube video

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.360
in 2026. So, if you like this type of

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.240
content, gently tap that like button,

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:44.720
and let's jump into it right now. Okay,

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.840
step one is to pick your preliminary

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.040
niche. Now, I want you to think about a

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.240
younger version of yourself, maybe 5

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.520
years ago or 10 years ago. What did you

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:55.840
struggle with back then? What cost you

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.920
time, money, and energy? What do you

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.000
wish that someone had told you? What

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.760
problems did you have that you were able

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.920
to overcome? Now, once you've picked

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:06.000
your niche, you need to clearly define

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.280
who you're helping and what problem

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.840
you're helping them solve. This is

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.040
what's called a niche hypothesis

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.440
statement, and it goes something like

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:15.640
this. I help X overcome Y, or I help X

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.800
do Y. So, in the case of my brother, he

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.280
helps younger people choose the right

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:21.040
trade career for them. Now, this is a

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.400
very important step, but realize it's

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.680
preliminary. You're not stuck here

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.040
forever, but it's important that you

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.760
actually do this step. That right there

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:30.320
is your niche. You're not starting from

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:32.200
zero, you're starting from experience.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.320
And there are thousands of people out

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.560
there who are exactly where you used to

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.160
be. They need what you already know.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:40.080
Now, there's one important thing. This

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.680
is your preliminary niche, not your

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.120
final one. For instance, I switched my

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:46.280
niches at least 15 times. You're just

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:48.400
picking a direction to start moving. So,

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:49.640
don't overthink it. Just pick something

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:51.040
and keep going. In the case of my

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.960
brother, he'd been working in the trades

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.960
for 30 years. And so, it made a lot of

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:57.120
sense for him to talk about getting into

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.880
the trades and which trade would be best

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.760
depending on you, your situation, and

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.680
your personality. Step two, get your

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.720
keywords. Now, we need to find out what

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:06.480
people are actually searching for. So,

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.679
the tool we're going to use is called

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.000
VidIQ. It's free. What you want to do is

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:13.760
go into VidIQ, and you actually get five

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.000
free questions to ask the VidIQ AI every

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.040
single month. So, you're going to put

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.560
your niche hypothesis statement into

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.000
VidIQ, and then ask it what keywords are

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.680
related. It's going to spit out a few

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.040
keywords, and you want to copy these and

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.880
save them. So, when you write down my

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:28.600
brother's niche, these are the keywords

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:30.560
that pop up. Step three, find three muse

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:32.520
videos on YouTube. This is the most

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.320
important step that most beginners skip.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:37.360
Before you create anything, you need

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.440
proof the topic already works. So, go on

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:41.400
YouTube and search the keywords that you

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:43.040
found one at a time. You're looking for

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.920
videos that hit all three of these

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.400
rules. One, the channel that posted the

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:49.880
video has less than 100,000 subscribers.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:52.360
Two, the video has at least 100,000

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:54.920
views. And three, the view to subscriber

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:57.000
ratio is at least five to one. Meaning,

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:59.120
if the channel has 20,000 subscribers,

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.440
the views have to be at least 100,000.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.920
And if the channel has 100,000

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.880
subscribers, the views have to be at

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.160
least 500,000. Now, why does this

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:08.040
matter? Because it means the topic is

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.720
bigger than the channel. The algorithm

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:11.680
pushed that video to people who had

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.800
never heard of that creator. And then,

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.680
when they saw that it was a small

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.920
creator, they watched anyways. Even

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:17.760
though that creator didn't have a big

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.560
audience or social proof, they still

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.360
chose to watch the video. And by finding

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.480
these types of videos, it makes it much

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:25.720
more likely that your video can do well,

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:27.240
too. So, find three videos that hit all

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.800
three of those rules, then pick your

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:30.480
favorite. That's your muse video. Here's

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.040
some examples of videos that we found

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.720
for my brother. And here's the one that

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.800
we picked. All right, quick break. I'm

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.640
hanging out with my brother Zach right

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.720
now. He's not a tech guy at all, and he

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:41.440
made $214 in a single day on YouTube.

