back to your regularly scheduled

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.640
programming. All right, step four is to

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:40.160
generate your title. Now, here's the

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:42.280
rule for your first video. Keep the

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.920
title 90% the same as the original.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.040
Don't reinvent it, don't try to be

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.680
clever. Just swap out small details to

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:49.200
make it fit your niche. So, the creator

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.400
you're modeling already did the hard

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:53.560
work. They tested that title. It worked.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:55.920
Your job right now is not to innovate.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.520
Your job is to execute. Learn the rules

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.480
first, then you can break them later.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.920
Now, the only thing you're going to be

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:03.040
copying here is the idea of the video.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:05.160
But, the idea is expressed in the title,

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:07.600
so your title needs to be very similar,

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:09.520
90 to 95% the same. If you change your

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.480
title up too much, it might end up being

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:13.640
a completely different idea. So, don't

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:14.960
do that. So, here's the original video,

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.720
and here's my brother's title. You can

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.800
see that they are very similar. Just a

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:20.640
few words are swapped out. However,

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:22.520
everything else about the video is

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:24.480
completely different. And this leads us

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.480
to step five. Generate your thumbnail

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:28.200
words. Most thumbnails need text on

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:29.560
them. So, you want to have text, but

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.720
keep it short, three to four words

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:32.480
maximum. You can see that in my

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:34.520
brother's thumbnail, he has four words

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:37.000
and one number. Also, the words need to

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.800
be bold and easy to read even on a small

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.680
phone screen. And it needs to match the

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:42.440
energy of your title. Think of it this

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:44.160
way. Your thumbnail gets them to look,

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.320
and your title gets them to click. But,

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:48.760
both of them need to work together. Step

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:50.960
six, write your scripts. Now, here you

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.720
have two different options. Option A is

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:54.040
the outline method. You write bullet

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.720
points of what you want to cover, and

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:57.720
you just talk about it naturally on

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:59.360
camera. This is what I recommend to most

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.960
people that are doing their first video.

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:03.080
It keeps you sounding like a real human

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.320
being because most people, if they try

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:07.280
to read the script word for word, sound

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:09.080
kind of like a robot. Option B is the

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:10.680
full script method. Write out every

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:12.440
single word, then read it on a

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.720
teleprompter or from your screen. Now,

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:15.640
this is better for some people,

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.840
especially if you freeze up on camera or

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:18.640
if you lose your train of thought

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:20.280
easily. Neither option is wrong, just

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.720
pick the one that fits you and move

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:23.640
forward. Now, you can either have your

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:25.280
script very close to your camera, like

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:26.640
you can elevate your computer right next

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:28.280
to your camera, maybe even above your

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:29.840
camera, and just look at it. Or, if you

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.160
want to get really fancy, you can use a

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:32.720
teleprompter. Now, when you're writing

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:35.040
out a full script, you can definitely

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:37.360
use AI for this. My most recommended

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.640
method is to basically just have what's

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:40.840
known as a yap session with AI, where

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:42.640
you kind of just tell it what your

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:44.600
thoughts are on the subject, and then

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:46.000
have it fill in the rest. We actually

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.880
have an AI that we created for our

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:49.400
clients that's designed to do exactly

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:51.080
this, where you literally just talk to

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:52.840
it and it writes the script for you. And

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:54.440
that's exactly what my brother did. The

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:56.440
script writing process took him less

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:58.240
than 15 minutes. And he decided to use a

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.720
teleprompter to read the script in his

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.000
first video. Now, I know there's more to

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.240
script writing than that, and if you're

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:04.280
interested in learning more about that,

